        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Small black flying bugs in a house are almost always telling you where something wet and organic is. Fungus gnats mean overwatered soil, so let it dry. Drain flies mean a dirty drain, so find it with tape and scrub it with a brush. Phorid flies mean decay somewhere, so clean the obvious sources and call a plumber if large numbers persist.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Flying ants and termite swarmers are the exception, because they point to a colony rather than a damp spot. Learn the antennae, waist and wing checks, and if they are termites, get an inspection rather than reaching for a spray.
          </p>
        </div>

